hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-29 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-29 = unlines (cons "The fiber of histories compatible with a reading, and the warrant over that whole fiber, is how a knowledge graph should represent incomplete knowledge. A source that reports something is an" (cons "observation. What follows from the report is whatever holds for every state of affairs compatible with it. Missing" (cons "information is kept as the family of possibilities, not compressed into a number. Combining two sources intersects" (cons "their fibers, and refining an observation shrinks the fiber, so a conclusion established on the coarser fiber stays" (cons "established on the finer one. When a probability structure really is given, it is extra information that further" (cons "reasoning can use. It isn't a stand-in for the information that's absent." nil))))))
